1
00:03:53,793 --> 00:03:59,793
The days are numbered.

2
00:07:47,586 --> 00:07:53,586
28 Days Later is a horror, thriller, science
fiction film directed by Danny Boyle.

3
00:11:41,379 --> 00:11:47,379
Twenty-eight days after a killer virus was accidentally unleashed from a British research facility, a small group
of London survivors are caught in a desperate struggle to protect themselves from the infected.

4
00:15:35,172 --> 00:15:41,172
Carried by animals and humans, the virus turns those it infects into
homicidal maniacs -- and it's absolutely impossible to contain.

5
00:19:28,965 --> 00:19:34,965
Jim, played by Cillian Murphy.

6
00:23:22,758 --> 00:23:28,758
Selena, played by Naomie Harris.

7
00:27:16,551 --> 00:27:22,551
Frank, played by Brendan Gleeson.

8
00:31:10,344 --> 00:31:16,344
Hannah, played by Megan Burns.

9
00:35:04,137 --> 00:35:10,137
Major Henry West, played by Christopher Eccleston.

10
00:38:57,931 --> 00:39:03,931
Mark, played by Noah Huntley.

11
00:42:51,724 --> 00:42:57,724
28 Days Later (sometimes stylised with an ellipsis as 28 Days Later...) is a 2002 British
post-apocalyptic horror film directed by Danny Boyle and written by Alex Garland.

12
00:46:45,517 --> 00:46:51,517
It stars Cillian Murphy as a bicycle courier who awakens from a coma to discover that the accidental
release of a highly contagious, aggression-inducing virus has caused the breakdown of society.

13
00:50:39,310 --> 00:50:45,310
Naomie Harris, Christopher Eccleston, Megan Burns, and
Brendan Gleeson appear in supporting roles.

14
00:54:33,103 --> 00:54:39,103
Garland took inspiration from George A.

15
00:58:26,896 --> 00:58:32,896
Romero's Night of the Living Dead film series and John
Wyndham's 1951 novel The Day of the Triffids.

16
01:02:20,689 --> 01:02:26,689
Filming took place in various locations in the United Kingdom in 2001.

17
01:06:14,482 --> 01:06:20,482
The crew filmed for brief periods during early mornings and temporarily closed streets to
capture recognisable and typically busy areas when they were deserted.

18
01:10:08,275 --> 01:10:14,275
John Murphy composed an original soundtrack for the film, with
other instrumental songs by Brian Eno, Godspeed You!

19
01:14:02,068 --> 01:14:08,068
Black Emperor, and other artists.

20
01:17:55,862 --> 01:18:01,862
28 Days Later was released on 1 November 2002 in the United Kingdom by Fox
Searchlight Pictures to generally positive reviews and commercial success.

21
01:21:49,655 --> 01:21:55,655
Grossing $82.8 million worldwide on a budget of $8 million, it
became one of the most profitable horror films of 2002.

22
01:25:43,448 --> 01:25:49,448
Reviewers praised Boyle's direction, the cast's performances,
Garland's screenplay, the atmosphere and soundtrack.

23
01:29:37,241 --> 01:29:43,241
Despite Boyle not considering it a zombie film, 28 Days Later is credited with reinvigorating the genre and influencing
a revival in it a decade after its release, with its fast-running infected and character-driven drama.

24
01:33:31,034 --> 01:33:37,034
It has been featured in several "best-of" film lists.

25
01:37:24,827 --> 01:37:30,827
The film's success launched its titular film series, featuring three further installments, 28 Weeks
Later (2007), 28 Years Later (2025), and 28 Years Later: The Bone Temple (2026).

26
01:41:18,620 --> 01:41:24,620
A wider franchise also includes the graphic novel 28 Days Later: The Aftermath
(2007), and the comic book series 28 Days Later (2009–2011).

27
01:45:12,413 --> 01:45:18,413
The film explores themes of daughter, taxi, london,
england, submachine gun, gas station.

28
01:49:06,206 --> 01:49:12,206
The tone is dark and thought_provoking and intense.
